[
	# XIME Graphics — System Overview

	XIME.Graphics is the shader and effects layer of the XIME framework for the Elarion ecosystem. It delivers real-time blur surfaces, liquid crystal effects, and kinetic interaction shaders tuned for 60–120fps budgets.

	## Blur Engines (`xime.graphics.shader.blur`)
	Loc: `src/main/java/xime/graphics/shader/blur`

	* **Glass.java** — Real-time stack blur engine with explicit 120fps tuning levers: fewer pixels touched and more cores touching them at once.
	* **Crystal.java** — High-transparency liquid crystal effect using cached instance blur that reuses buffers instead of reallocating every call, caches applyToBitmap() meshes/gradients, and blurs oversized bitmaps at reduced resolution.

	## Interaction Shaders (`xime.graphics.shader.bloom` / `dash`)
	Loc: `src/main/java/xime/graphics/shader/bloom`, `src/main/java/xime/graphics/shader/dash`

	* **SwipeBloom.java** — Highlight-softening interaction effect drawing soft edge glow and gradient-based fade shapes.
	* **SwipeDash.java** — Kinetic dash trail visualizer built on swoosh logic: a stretching oval that moves vertically.
]
